  "preamble": "The retroflex flap /ɽ/ (ড়, ঢ়) merges with the alveolar tap [ɾ] of /r/ (র) in Bengali. The distinction is weakened in western and central dialects and fully lost in eastern (Vanga) dialects, where both rhotics are realized as the alveolar tap [ɾ] or the approximant [ɹ]; Dhaka speech has [ɹ]. Wiktionary records Vanga পড়া [ˈpɔɾaˑ] as a homophone of পরা, and the Rarh (standard) pronunciations of বড় 'big', বাড়ি 'house' and গাড়ি 'car' include variants with [ɾ] beside [ɽ]. Historically /ɽ/ is the non-initial allophone of /ɖ/.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Bengali (Vanga / Eastern)",
      "languageFamily": "Eastern Indo-Aryan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "পড়া /pɔɽa/ (Rarh)",
          "to": "/pɔɾa/ [ˈpɔɾaˑ]",
          "note": "Wiktionary lists পরা as a homophone in Vanga."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Bengali (Rarh)",
      "languageFamily": "Eastern Indo-Aryan",
